@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Variant — the same banking domain shown as an object diagram (instances) and a class diagram (types) side by side.
'   usecase:      Contrast instance-snapshot (object diagram) with type-definition (class diagram).
'   complexity:   simple
'   domain:       Banking
' ============================================================================
title Example Object Diagram Variant - Object vs Class

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' LEFT frame: OBJECT diagram — concrete runtime instances with slot values
'             and links between specific objects.
' RIGHT frame: CLASS diagram — abstract type definitions with typed members
'              and associations between classifiers.
' The two views describe the SAME domain at different meta-levels: the class
' diagram is the schema/blueprint; the object diagram is one snapshot of data
' that conforms to that schema.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

' ===== OBJECT DIAGRAM (instances) =========================================
together {
  object "john:Customer" as oJohn {
    name = "John Smith"
    customerId = 42
  }

  object "acct:Account" as oAcct {
    accountId = 1001
    balance = 1500.00
  }

  oJohn "1" --> "owns *" oAcct
}

' ===== CLASS DIAGRAM (types) ==============================================
together {
  class Customer <<class>> {
    - name : String
    - customerId : int
    + openAccount() : Account
  }

  class Account <<class>> {
    - accountId : int
    - balance : Money
    + deposit(amount : Money)
  }

  Customer "1" --> "owns *" Account
}

' --- Divider note --------------------------------------------------------
note top of oJohn
  <b>OBJECT DIAGRAM</b>
  Instances with concrete slot values.
  "john:Customer" is ONE customer.
  Links connect specific objects.
end note

note top of Customer
  <b>CLASS DIAGRAM</b>
  Type definitions with typed members.
  Customer is the CLASS for ALL customers.
  Associations connect classifiers.
end note

note bottom of Customer
  <b>Instance-snapshot vs type-definition</b>
  The class diagram (right) defines WHAT fields and links are possible.
  The object diagram (left) shows WHAT the values are RIGHT NOW.
  Every object must conform to its class: john.name is a String because
  Customer.name : String; the john->acct link is legal because the
  Customer "owns" Account association permits it.
end note

@enduml
